WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.687 --> 00:00:04.987
This arrow is a qubit.

2
00:00:04.987 --> 00:00:08.257
Straight up means zero, straight down means one,

3
00:00:08.257 --> 00:00:11.287
and anywhere in between is a superposition:

4
00:00:11.287 --> 00:00:13.177
a blend of both at once.

5
00:00:13.920 --> 00:00:19.323
The blend is described by two amplitudes, one for zero and one for one.

6
00:00:19.323 --> 00:00:22.790
Square them, and you get the odds of measuring each.

7
00:00:23.553 --> 00:00:26.033
But an amplitude is more than a size.

8
00:00:26.033 --> 00:00:30.796
It also points in a direction, its phase, like the hand of a clock.

9
00:00:30.796 --> 00:00:35.813
Turn that hand, and the odds of a measurement do not change at all.

10
00:00:36.553 --> 00:00:38.572
Phase matters when amplitudes meet.

11
00:00:38.572 --> 00:00:40.613
A Hadamard gate adds them up:

12
00:00:40.613 --> 00:00:45.373
hands pointing the same way reinforce, opposite hands cancel.

13
00:00:45.373 --> 00:00:50.743
That is interference, and it turns a hidden phase into an answer you can measure.
